---
import './figure.css';
import './session-card.css';
---

<figure class="post-fig f6" aria-describedby="f6-desc">
  <figcaption>
    <p class="post-fig-title">figure 7: going back, recall and ask</p>
    <p class="muted">
      recall greps the archive with no inference; ask puts one question to an archived thread,
      and only the answer comes back.
    </p>
  </figcaption>
  <div id="f6-desc" class="sr-only"><slot /></div>

  <div class="stack">
    <section class="sess" aria-label="recall example">
      <header class="sess-h"><span>main line, after the fold</span><b>recall</b></header>
      <ol class="sess-b">
        <li class="ln ctx note">
          <span class="who">note</span><span class="msg"
            >builds. regenerated src/client from the OpenAPI spec … <span class="hd">↪ b2e4</span
            ></span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln ctx">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg">frontend: wire the export button</span>
        </li>
        <li class="ln call">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg"
            ><span class="fn">recall</span>("TS2322")</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln tool">
          <span class="who">tool</span>
          <div class="msg res hits">
            <span class="hd">b2e4</span><span class="span">fold "make it build, 2 rounds"</span>
            <span></span><span class="k">t5</span><span class="k">tool</span><span class="t"
              >src/client/api.ts(12,5): error <mark>TS2322</mark>: Type 'string' is not assignable
              to type 'number'.</span
            >
            <span></span><span class="k">t6</span><span class="k">thinking</span><span
              class="t think">"every <mark>TS2322</mark> is under src/client/, nothing in src/jobs"{' '}<span class="cm">(when the provider returns it)</span></span
            >
            <span></span><span class="k">t8</span><span class="k">agent</span><span class="t"
              >the errors are all in the generated client, regenerating it{' '}
              <span class="cm">(reply to t5)</span></span
            >
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ln call">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg"
            ><span class="fn">recall</span>("SKIP LOCKED")</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln tool">
          <span class="who">tool</span>
          <div class="msg res hits">
            <span class="hd">a91c</span><span class="k"></span><span class="k">note</span><span
              class="t"
              >claim query in src/jobs/claim.ts. only valid inside a transaction: FOR UPDATE{' '}
              <mark>SKIP LOCKED</mark> holds the row lock until commit.</span
            >
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="cost">
        <span
          >cost: no inference. ~300 tokens appended to the main line × $3/MTok ≈{' '}
          <span class="num">$0.001</span>, warm or cold</span
        >
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sess" aria-label="ask example">
      <header class="sess-h"><span>main line</span><b>ask</b></header>
      <ol class="sess-b">
        <li class="ln ctx">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg">frontend: wire the export button</span>
        </li>
        <li class="ln call">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg"
            ><span class="fn">ask</span>("b2e4", "why regenerate instead of fixing the type in
            api.ts?")</span
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <section class="sess arc" aria-label="thread b2e4, asked off the main line">
            <header class="sess-h"><span>off the main line</span><b>thread b2e4</b></header>
            <ol class="sess-b">
              <li class="ln pe">
                <span class="who">B + E</span><span class="msg"
                  >system … t1 user … t4 $ pnpm build … t10 ✓ <span class="num">~64K</span>{' '}
                  <span class="swap cm"
                    ><span class="warm">(cache warm: read at cached price)</span><span class="cold"
                      >(cache cold: read at full price)</span
                    ></span
                  ></span
                >
              </li>
              <li class="ln">
                <span class="who">tools</span><span class="msg cm"
                  >same tools block as the thread, so the cache still matches</span
                >
              </li>
              <li class="ln user">
                <span class="who">ask</span><span class="msg"
                  >why regenerate instead of fixing the type in api.ts? answer without acting.{' '}
                  <span class="cm">(appended)</span></span
                >
              </li>
              <li class="ln">
                <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg cm"
                  >one step, writes the answer below</span
                >
              </li>
            </ol>
            <p class="sess-f">dropped after the answer; b2e4 stays in the archive as it was</p>
          </section>
        </li>
        <li class="ln tool ans">
          <span class="who">tool</span><span class="msg res"
            >api.ts is generated from the OpenAPI spec; a hand edit is overwritten on the next
            generate. The spec had changed and the client had not. If the type is wrong, the fix
            is in the spec, not the client.</span
          >
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="cost">
        <span>only the answer enters the main line (~50 tokens)</span>
        <fieldset class="chips">
          <legend class="sr-only">cache state</legend>
          <label class="check"
            ><input type="checkbox" id="f6-warm" />cache still warm (within 5 min)</label
          >
        </fieldset>
        <span
          >cost: re-read B + E <span class="opt w"
            >warm 64K × $0.30/MTok ≈ <span class="num">$0.019</span></span
          > · <span class="opt c">cold 64K × $3/MTok ≈ <span class="num">$0.19</span></span>{' '}
          + ~50 output tokens × $15/MTok ≈ <span class="num">$0.001</span></span
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p class="muted f6-prices">Prices assumed: $3 input, $0.30 cached read, $15 output per million tokens.</p>
</figure>

<style>

  /* fig 6 */
  .f6 .f6-prices {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .f6 .stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .f6 .ctx :is(.who, .msg, .hd) {
    color: var(--muted-ink);
  }
  .f6 .call .msg {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .f6 .fn {
    color: var(--link-ink);
  }
  .f6 .hits {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4ch 3ch 8ch minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0 1.5ch;
  }
  .f6 .hits .span {
    grid-column: 2 / -1;
    color: var(--muted-ink);
  }
  .f6 .hits .k {
    color: var(--comment-ink);
  }
  .f6 .hits .t {
    color: var(--muted-ink);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .f6 .hits .think {
    font-style: italic;
  }
  /* Narrow column: the matched text gets its own row under handle/turn/kind. */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .f6 .hits {
      grid-template-columns: 4ch 3ch minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .f6 .hits .t {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      padding: 0 0 2px 2ch;
    }
  }
  .f6 mark {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--metric-ink) 22%, transparent);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .f6 .arc {
    margin: 3px 10px 3px calc(7ch + 20px);
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in oklab, var(--loop) 55%, var(--rule));
    background: var(--page-bg);
  }
  .f6 .arc .sess-h,
  .f6 .arc .sess-f {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--loop) 35%, var(--rule));
  }
  .f6 .arc .sess-b {
    padding: 4px 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .f6 .arc {
      margin-left: 10px;
    }
  }
  .f6 .pe {
    border-left-color: var(--metric-ink);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--metric-ink) 9%, transparent);
    transition:
      border-color 0.2s,
      background-color 0.2s;
  }
  .f6:has(#f6-warm:checked) .pe {
    border-left-color: var(--link-ink);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--link-ink) 9%, transparent);
  }
  /* Both tags share one grid cell, so the longer one always reserves the space. */
  .f6 .swap {
    display: inline-grid;
  }
  .f6 .swap > * {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
  }
  .f6 .warm,
  .f6:has(#f6-warm:checked) .cold {
    visibility: hidden;
  }
  .f6:has(#f6-warm:checked) .warm {
    visibility: visible;
  }
  .f6 .ans .msg {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .f6 .cost {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--rule);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--comment-ink);
  }
  .f6 .cost .chips {
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  /* Both prices stay on screen; the checkbox only says which one applies. */
  .f6 .opt {
    opacity: 0.55;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }
  .f6 .opt .num {
    color: var(--comment-ink);
  }
  .f6:has(#f6-warm:checked) .opt.w,
  .f6:has(#f6-warm:not(:checked)) .opt.c {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .f6:has(#f6-warm:checked) .opt.w .num,
  .f6:has(#f6-warm:not(:checked)) .opt.c .num {
    color: var(--metric-ink);
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .f6 :is(.pe, .opt) {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
